            "ObjectName": {
              "value": "<b>Original</b> \u2013 <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proclamation_of_the_Republic_(Brazil)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Proclamation of the Republic (Brazil)\">Proclamation of the Republic</a></b>, 1893, oil on canvas by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benedito_Calixto\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Benedito Calixto\">Benedito Calixto</a> (1853-1927).\nThe proclamation of the Republic took place in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rio_de_Janeiro\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Rio de Janeiro\">Rio de Janeiro</a>, then capital of the Empire of Brazil, when a group of military officers of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brazilian_Army\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Brazilian Army\">Brazilian Army</a>, led by Marshal <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deodoro_da_Fonseca\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Deodoro da Fonseca\">Deodoro da Fonseca</a>, staged a coup d'\u00e9tat without the use of violence, deposing the Emperor of Brazil, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dom_Pedro_II\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Dom Pedro II\">Dom Pedro II</a>, and the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prime_Minister_of_Brazil\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Prime Minister of Brazil\">President of the Council of Ministers of the Empire</a>, the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viscount_of_Ouro_Preto\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Viscount of Ouro Preto\">Viscount of Ouro Preto</a>.",
              "source": "commons-desc-page"
            },
